<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Badi IV</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. <a href="/years/1724">1724</a>–<a href="/years/1762">1762</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as Badi IV Abu Shulukh</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Badi IV, called Abu Shulukh, was the last Funj sultan of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/funj-sultanate-of-sennar">Sennar</a> to hold real power, reigning from 1724 to 1762. His forces defeated an Ethiopian invasion under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iyasu-ii">Iyasu II</a> in 1744, but his reliance on new favourites alienated the nobility. In 1762 he was deposed by his general <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muhammad-abu-likaylik">Muhammad Abu Likaylik</a>, after which the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hamaj">Hamaj</a> regents ruled in the sultans' name.</p></div>
